From: HomoXterm contributors
Subject: [PATCH] accept ssh-rsa public blobs for RSA-SHA2 host keys

RFC 8332 changes the negotiated signature algorithm to rsa-sha2-256 or
rsa-sha2-512, but the RSA public-key blob remains encoded with the ssh-rsa
key format from RFC 4253.  Do not tie acceptance of that public-key format
to SHA-1 signature support.  LIBSSH2_RSA_SHA1 remains disabled by the
OHCRYPTO backend.

--- a/src/hostkey.c
+++ b/src/hostkey.c
@@ -91,5 +91,5 @@ hostkey_method_ssh_rsa_init(LIBSSH2_SESSION * session,
     /* we accept one of 3 header types */
-#if LIBSSH2_RSA_SHA1
+#if LIBSSH2_RSA_SHA1 || LIBSSH2_RSA_SHA2
     if(type_len == 7 && strncmp("ssh-rsa", (char *)type, 7) == 0) {
         /* ssh-rsa */
     }
